# Terraform Conventions

## Naming

Pattern: `${var.name_prefix}-<resource>-<type>`

All lowercase, hyphens only — no underscores in resource names. Examples:

- `demo-s3files-filesystem-role`
- `demo-s3files-mt-sg`
- `demo-s3files-compute-sg`
- `demo-s3files-instance-profile`

Module source references always use `./modules/<name>` (relative path, no registry prefix).

## for_each over count

Use `for_each` when creating multiple instances of the same resource type with independent lifecycles (e.g. mount targets per subnet). Use `count` only for binary on/off toggling.

```hcl
# Good — independent lifecycle per subnet
resource "aws_s3files_mount_target" "this" {
  for_each = toset(var.subnet_ids)
  subnet_id = each.value
}

# Good — binary feature flag
resource "aws_iam_instance_profile" "compute" {
  count = var.compute_type == "ec2" ? 1 : 0
}
```

## Security group rules

Never use inline `ingress` / `egress` blocks in `aws_security_group`. Always declare SGs without inline rules and attach rules via `aws_security_group_rule`. This avoids circular dependency errors when two SGs reference each other.

```hcl
# Good
resource "aws_security_group" "mount_target" { ... }
resource "aws_security_group" "compute" { ... }
resource "aws_security_group_rule" "nfs_ingress" {
  type                     = "ingress"
  security_group_id        = aws_security_group.mount_target.id
  source_security_group_id = aws_security_group.compute.id
  ...
}
```

## Variable types

Use `optional()` in object variables to allow partial configuration. Use `nullable = false` when a variable must not be null after defaulting.

```hcl
variable "kms_key_id" {
  type    = string
  default = null   # null means "use SSE-S3"
}
```

## IAM policies

Use `jsonencode()` for all inline IAM policy documents — never heredoc JSON strings. Use `concat()` to conditionally include statement blocks:

```hcl
policy = jsonencode({
  Statement = concat(
    [{ always_included_statement }],
    var.kms_key_arn != null ? [{ kms_statement }] : []
  )
})
```

## lifecycle blocks

Always add `create_before_destroy = true` to security groups to allow in-place replacement.

## depends_on

Add explicit `depends_on` only when a dependency cannot be inferred from resource references (e.g. IAM propagation delays between modules). Document why with a comment.

## terraform-docs

Every `variables.tf` and `outputs.tf` variable/output must have a `description` field. Every module `README.md` must contain the terraform-docs markers:

```markdown
<!-- BEGIN_TF_DOCS -->
<!-- END_TF_DOCS -->
```

## Outputs

Re-export all key IDs and ARNs from modules in the root `outputs.tf`. Outputs that are conditionally null must document the condition in their `description`.

## Provider version

Root `versions.tf`:
```hcl
required_providers {
  aws = {
    source  = "hashicorp/aws"
    version = ">= 6.40"   # minimum for aws_s3files_* native resources
  }
}
```

Example `versions.tf` should pin the same floor.
